# Managed by host/ansible/roles/chrony. The time contract is coordinator#11.
#
# A drop-in rather than a replacement chrony.conf, so the vendor's upstream sources
# stay as they are and work whenever the bench network is up.

# The one seconds-source, served by coord-rtc-feed over a SOCK datagram. ONE, because
# the PPS refclock below can lock= to exactly one refid -- a second seconds-source
# could disagree with the one the pulse is paired to and be marked a falseticker.
#
# Its offset is whatever the best truth available is: real UTC measured through the
# FC's TIMESYNC and SYSTEM_TIME when the FC is up with a fix, and the DS3234's own
# registers when it is not. The chip is never written, because that resets its
# countdown chain and makes one second the wrong length.
#
# precision 2e-3 is the chip path's error: coord-rtc finds the second boundary by
# polling the seconds register, so the poll interval bounds it. The FC path is better
# and is not distinguished here; doing that wants two refids and a lock= decision
# rather than a tighter number.
refclock SOCK {{ coord_rtc_chrony_sock }} refid DS32 precision 2e-3 poll 4

# The buffered 1 Hz on GPIO24. lock=DS32 pairs each edge with an RTC sample: the RTC
# says which second, the edge says where the second starts. Without a lock chrony
# discards every pulse until it is already synchronised to something.
refclock PPS /dev/pps0 refid PPS lock=DS32 precision 1e-7 poll 2

# Serve the campods over the USB gadget network. They have no connection to the
# DS3234 and no FC link, so this plus their own buffered PPS leg is their whole time
# source.
#
# Derived from the coordinator's address rather than a second subnet variable, which
# vars/gadget-net.yml says not to add. The role asserts the prefix is 24 so this
# derivation cannot quietly become wrong.
allow {{ campod_gadget_coordinator_ip.rsplit('.', 1)[0] }}.0/{{ campod_gadget_prefix }}
